                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَانَ لَهُ</span></b> 
                        , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَهِينُ</span>, <i>He treated him with
gentleness,</i> or <i>blandishment;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَارَاهُ</span>. (Aboo-Is-hák, in TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عن</span>; but only the imp.,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِنْ لَهُ</span>, is there mentioned, said to be with
kesr.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَزَّ</span>, near the end, p. 2031, and the
distinction there made between <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِنْ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُنْ</span>.

